From 79401c26b104c9dd1e89e34de60f7f04dd20d9f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:54:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix avatar picker grid width, remove ambient glow tint, use
 shared Dropdown for skill comparison

- Avatar picker's expanded panel now sizes to its content instead of
  stretching full-width, so the fixed-size swatch grid doesn't leave a
  large empty gap.
- Added a scoped .no-ambient-glow override that drops the lavender
  radial-gradient wash baked into surface-glass-1/2/3 while keeping the
  blur/shadow/border, and applied it to the run history table, master
  roster, deliverables panel (including the Call Intelligence header),
  every surface-glass surface under dashboard/runs/[id], and the
  engagement skill panels rendered under dashboard/engagements/[id]/skills
  (leak-map schedule, rep findings, win-back pipeline/revenue/cadence,
  pile-on pipeline/ad creative briefs).
- Swapped the analytics Skill comparison section's native <select>
  pickers for the shared Dropdown component (@/components/ui/dropdown).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011PX9qLTKPtXba6ncjAwLyN
